# Testing / Verification
- Define expected and failure behavior before implementation.
- Discover commands from repository config, CI, manifests and scripts; never invent project-standard commands.
- Run narrowest relevant checks first: syntax/static -> targeted unit -> targeted integration -> affected module/package -> type/lint -> build/package -> smoke/E2E/runtime as relevant.
- Add regression coverage for bug fixes when a compatible framework exists.
- Test material negative/error paths and boundaries.
- Never weaken/skip/delete assertions merely to make tests green unless intended product behavior changed.
- Distinguish patch-caused failures from pre-existing failures.
- Reinspect diff after verification.
- Final report must state exactly what ran, results, and what could not run.
- Static analysis alone does not prove runtime behavior; a build alone does not prove end-to-end behavior.
